      "Context matters enormously here. A long rejection wick at a level nobody's watching means very little. The exact same wick at a widely-observed round number, right where a swing high sits, carries far more weight \u2014 because it's evidence that real, meaningful liquidity was actually defended there.",
      "An engulfing candle \u2014 where one candle's body completely swallows the previous candle's body \u2014 often marks a genuine shift in short-term control, especially when it happens directly at a key level rather than in open space.",
      "The logic: for the second candle's body to fully engulf the first, the side that was previously losing had to not just stop the move, but reverse it with enough conviction to erase the entire prior candle's progress and then some, all within a single period. That's a much stronger statement than a simple wick rejection, and it's why engulfing candles at a key level are worth paying particular attention to.",
      "How price approaches and reacts to a level tells a different story depending on speed. A slow, grinding push through a level \u2014 small candles, steady progress, no dramatic rejection \u2014 often means the level is gradually being absorbed and will eventually give way. A fast, violent spike through a level that immediately reverses is a completely different animal: a classic liquidity sweep, the exact concept this curriculum builds toward next.",
      "Learning to distinguish these two in real time \u2014 before you know which one it turned out to be \u2014 is one of the higher-skill reads in this entire curriculum. A useful starting heuristic: the slow grind usually shows multiple candles making incremental progress toward the level with relatively small ranges, while the sweep shows one or two candles covering an unusually large distance very quickly, well beyond the average range of the candles around it.",
      "Everything from this chapter and the last one combines into a single practical skill: identify a level worth watching, then read exactly how price behaves when it gets there \u2014 the wick length, whether an engulfing pattern forms, and how fast the approach was. That combined read is far more informative than any one signal alone, and it's the foundation the rest of this curriculum's entry techniques are built on."
