      "Order blocks are one of the more subjective concepts in this curriculum to apply consistently, precisely because the checklist involves several conditions rather than one clean objective rule. The fix is the same one from earlier chapters: apply the checklist mechanically, every time, rather than eyeballing a candle and deciding after the fact that it \"looks like\" an order block because you already wanted to take the trade."
